# shellcheck shell=bash
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  app.env — ziptask service configuration
#
#  Vendored from synaptomind/deploy, which is itself vendored from
#  bun-templates/deploy.
#    upstream: https://forgejo.home.lan/authelia/bun-templates
#              commit 89be318daf8adab5ddca957162b3b7df8429e725
#    copied from: /mnt/external/zum/PROJECTS/remote/synaptomind deploy/, re-vendored
#              for task #1136 (HEALTH_OK_VALUES quoting, SERVICE_GROUP, update_source
#              ownership ordering, print_summary Config line) on top of the task
#              #1108 framework gaps and the epic #1105 work since 1a3a0d6.
#    sha256 at copy time — REGENERATED from the files shipped in THIS directory by
#    `sha256sum install.sh update.sh updater.sh uninstall.sh lib/common.sh
#    hooks/pre-update hooks/post-update app.env.example`.
#    These are the anti-drift record: an operator re-vendoring by the documented
#    procedure compares against them, so a stale value here reads as a tampered
#    tree. Regenerate them in the same commit as any re-vendor, never by hand.
#      install.sh       f63bc561869f942e4f542e5ae55e72ab571b63e7ddc32261f04d841ec5f8f77c
#      update.sh        a5f07f4c90becad686cceb90591cd4b1efc33464142f626f4c410c569babbce1
#      updater.sh       b6296125130db4807852e3d03dff306974c7de741898bbd6bcdb67b0c91c5179
#      uninstall.sh     b67cab644269a85efb069a4f5144f0033b86d56f802ae642f5fb528608b2d5bb
#      lib/common.sh    19ea24a38c8f279557b8165f5de1ab86672eb881ca80bbcf56a37b9521c18451
#      hooks/pre-update 0c92239e858a50573a200404a5c74428c17c265ad1b6d0b746db0f67b037cc90
#      hooks/post-update 3c930e1d6db6c3d4268d6bb2fa7c8c823abed64d312984796e7c761c315a08ab
#      app.env.example  744f97079c9e993f3feaa0943df96cd75dacfad752704f9b07598d66cd79992a
#
#  Local deviations from the vendored framework (see the epic #1105 ADR,
#  plans/2026-10-01-unify-deploy-framework-adr.md §4, and its addendum
#  plans/2026-10-01-unify-deploy-framework-adr-addendum-config-home.md §"ziptask"):
#    * install.sh  — DEPLOY_RAW_URL default + the one-liner in its header point at
#                    zumik3-del/ziptask instead of zumik3-del/synaptomind.
#                    --port and --dir are real (task #2245): a seeded
#                    settings.json has its port and dbPath aligned, and --dir
#                    re-homes DATA_DIR plus the two strings derived from it
#                    (apply_overrides) instead of moving the payload alone.
#    * updater.sh  — staging dir prefix is ${APP_NAME}-updater, not a literal.
#    * update.sh   — heals the RUN_DIR ownership boundary on an existing host:
#                    apply_run_dir_ownership runs after the payload swap, so a
#                    host that updates instead of re-installing ends up with the
#                    root-owned deploy tree too (task #2245).
#    * uninstall.sh — the helper scripts are removed through run_root when the
#                    plain rm is refused: RUN_DIR is root-owned since #2245.
#    * lib/common.sh — adds release-asset SHA-256 verification (issue #38,
#                    commit 701448a): binary_stage_payload() fetches the
#                    asset's .sha256 and aborts on a mismatch; a missing
#                    checksum only warns. Also (task #2245): resolve_target_user
#                    refuses a SERVICE_USER that does not exist on the host,
#                    resolve_port reads CONFIG_FILE so the health gate polls the
#                    port the service binds, and apply_run_dir_ownership hands
#                    RUN_DIR to root:<service-group> (0750 dirs and scripts,
#                    0640 app.env) instead of to the service user; its one-level
#                    heal refuses symlinks, so a planted link cannot redirect a
#                    root chown/chmod at an arbitrary target.
#    * hooks/pre-update — resolve_db_paths reads ziptask's settings.json "dbPath"
#                    instead of synaptomind's config.json "path"/"logDbPath";
#                    it now looks in DATA_DIR first (addendum R1).
#    * app.env     — the settings file is seeded into DATA_DIR (SEED_FILES_DATA),
#                    not into the payload tree (addendum R1), and CONFIG_FILE
#                    declares that home — now read by resolve_port(); SERVICE_USER
#                    is empty so a host without an `opencode` account installs,
#                    and HEALTH_URL is derived from the effective port.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Identity ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
APP_NAME="ziptask"
APP_DESC="ziptask — MCP task tracker"

# ── Distribution ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "binary" installs the published release tarball: no bun, no node_modules, no
# git checkout on the host (ADR 0001-style self-contained payload).
DIST="binary"

# ── binary mode ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Asset URL = ${RELEASES_BASE}/${TAG}/${ASSET_PATTERN}
RELEASES_BASE="https://github.com/zumik3-del/ziptask/releases/download"
# The LIST endpoint, not /releases/latest: /latest silently excludes prereleases
# and cannot express CHECKOUT_POLICY. Unauthenticated = 60 requests/hour per IP,
# so a 403/429 surfaces as an explicit error naming the --version <tag> remedy.
RELEASE_API="https://api.github.com/repos/zumik3-del/ziptask/releases?per_page=30"
# SINGLE QUOTES ARE REQUIRED: load_app_env() sources this file, so double quotes
# would expand ${APP_NAME}/${TAG}/${OS}/${ARCH} here and leave render_template()
# nothing to substitute. Same for APP_VERSION_CMD, whose ${BIN} is set by
# app_version() at call time.
ASSET_PATTERN='${APP_NAME}-${TAG}-${OS}-${ARCH}.tar.gz'
# src/index.ts:25-27 prints "ziptask <version>"; app_version() strips the app
# name, so the gate compares the bare version against the tag.
APP_VERSION_CMD='${BIN} --version'

# ── binary mode: payload shape ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The release tarball (see .github/workflows/release.yml, "Pack release
# tarball") holds exactly one top-level directory containing the single
# `ziptask` executable. These four lists are that shape, and the framework's
# defaults are synaptomind's, so ziptask names its own here.
BINARY_SUPPORTED_PLATFORMS="linux-x86_64"
BINARY_REQUIRED_FILES="ziptask"
BINARY_ROLLBACK_FILES="ziptask"
BINARY_SWAP_ORDER="ziptask"

# ── source mode (developer installs) ──────────────────────────────────────
# REPO_URL stays REQUIRED even in binary mode: the frozen updater.sh bootstrap
# shallow-clones the chosen tag to stage that release's own deploy/update.sh.
REPO_URL="https://github.com/zumik3-del/ziptask.git"
# stable | latest | prerelease select a release tag. A <branch> value is
# rejected in binary mode — a branch has no release asset.
CHECKOUT_POLICY="stable"

# ── Paths ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Canonical layout (ADR §1): code /opt/<app>, data /var/lib/<app>, state
# ~/.ziptask. RUN_DIR empty -> ${HOME}/.ziptask, which is where the helpers,
# hooks and app.env live — the deploy framework's own state, NOT the app's
# config: the service reads settings.json from DATA_DIR (see CONFIG_FILE).
#
# `--dir D` re-homes the two paths below WITHOUT editing this file: the payload
# goes to D and, while DATA_DIR still holds the canonical /var/lib/<app> value
# written here, the data dir and config move to D/data (install.sh:
# apply_overrides). A DATA_DIR the operator set to something else is kept as
# written.
#
# RUN_DIR is ROOT-OWNED once installed (task #2245): the directories and the
# helper scripts are 0750 root:<service-group>, app.env is 0640, so the service
# account can read and execute the deploy tooling but can never rewrite a script
# that a later `sudo` update runs. THE SERVICE ACCOUNT MUST BE A MEMBER OF THE
# SERVICE GROUP for that read/execute access — it is, by construction, when the
# group is the account's own primary group (the default).
INSTALL_DIR="/opt/ziptask"
DATA_DIR="/var/lib/ziptask"
RUN_DIR=""

# ── First-run seeding ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copied only when the destination does NOT exist, so an installed host keeps
# its own settings.json. settings.example.json carries the live shape: host
# 127.0.0.1, port 3005, leaseTtlMin 45, the full defaults block, and an
# absolute dbPath into DATA_DIR (so resolution never depends on the ./data
# symlink being present).
#
# DATA_DIR, not INSTALL_DIR (ADR addendum R1): the app's own config lives in its
# config home, beside its database. Seeding into the payload tree would put the
# operator's config where a binary swap writes and where the pre-update hook's
# RUN_DIR/INSTALL_DIR candidate list expects to find one — the confusion R1
# exists to remove. setup_data() runs before seed_files(), so DATA_DIR and the
# ./data symlink both exist by the time this copies.
SEED_FILES=""
SEED_FILES_DATA="settings.example.json:settings.json"
# ziptask has no secret to generate.
GENERATE_SECRET_IN=""

# ── Runtime / service ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EMPTY ON PURPOSE (task #2245): the fallback is the invoking account, or
# SUDO_USER when the install runs through sudo, so the one-liner works on a host
# that has no dedicated service account (there is nothing named `opencode` on a
# plain container). Set it to a dedicated account when one exists: it wins over
# SUDO_USER, and a USER NAME THAT DOES NOT EXIST ON THE HOST now aborts the
# install up front (resolve_target_user) instead of surfacing as a health-gate
# timeout that names only the port.
SERVICE_USER=""
# MUST be explicit: the binary-mode default (install.sh:default_exec_start) is
# ${INSTALL_DIR}/${APP_NAME} with no arguments, and ziptask reads its config
# only from --settings / ZIPTASK_SETTINGS (src/config.ts), so the default would
# silently run against ./data/ziptask.db under the unit's WorkingDirectory.
#
# --settings points at ${DATA_DIR}/settings.json, the R1 config home, which is
# what hooks/pre-update now searches FIRST — so the file the service reads and
# the file the hook reads dbPath from are one path, not two candidates.
EXEC_START="/opt/ziptask/ziptask --settings /var/lib/ziptask/settings.json"
# R1's declared config home, and it is LOAD-BEARING now (task #2245):
# resolve_port() reads it to decide which port the health gate polls on an
# EXISTING host, so the file the service reads, the file the hook reads dbPath
# from and the file the gate reads the port from are one path. Both this value
# and EXEC_START above are written as the canonical absolute paths, and
# install.sh `--dir` REWRITES THEM to the new root (apply_overrides) — a single
# string the unit renderer substitutes verbatim, so it is spelled out rather than
# built from ${DATA_DIR} at render time.
CONFIG_FILE="/var/lib/ziptask/settings.json"
PORT="3005"
# src/server.ts:152 answers GET /health with {"ok":true,"version":<app version>}.
# EMPTY means "derive it from the port the service actually binds"
# (http://127.0.0.1:<port>/health), which is what makes --port real: a literal
# here would keep polling 3005 whatever the flag said (task #2245).
HEALTH_URL=""
HEALTH_TIMEOUT="60"
# A SECOND health window, used only when HEALTH_TIMEOUT expired with no answer
# at all. A timeout is this run's own bound, not a fact about the service, so an
# update that cannot confirm the new version is reported UNVERIFIED instead of
# failed-with-a-rollback. 0 disables the re-check — not recommended.
HEALTH_CONFIRM_TIMEOUT="30"

# ── Health contract (framework gap (d), ADR §3d) ───────────────────────────
# ziptask's /health state key is the boolean "ok" (true when healthy), not a
# "status" string, so the framework's synaptomind-shaped defaults ("status" in
# ok|degraded) would declare a contract violation on a perfectly healthy
# service. The version check is enabled: /health carries "version", which the
# gate compares against the target release, so identity no longer rests on the
# ok flag alone.
HEALTH_STATUS_FIELD="ok"
HEALTH_OK_VALUES="true"
HEALTH_VERSION_FIELD="version"

# ── host requirements ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "no" — a binary host needs no bun at install time or at runtime.
REQUIRES_BUN="no"
# "git tar" — tar extracts the release payload, git is only the updater.sh
# bootstrap. sqlite3 is required by the pre-update hook, which refuses to swap
# the payload without a WAL-safe .backup of the database first.
SYSTEM_DEP_CMDS="git tar sqlite3"
HOOKS_DIR=""
LIB_RAW_URL="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zumik3-del/ziptask/main/deploy/lib/common.sh"